Donald Trump questioned the strengthening of sanctions against Russia after meeting with Xi Jinping.

Other news from last night:

Donald Trump called Joe Biden a freak and a criminal who should be in prison.;

In California, a large-scale theft was committed from a museum, where more than a thousand valuable exhibits, including jewelry of the indigenous peoples of America, were stolen.;

"That's how a child behaves. This is not how a responsible ruling party in the United States of America should behave," US Vice President Jay Dee Vance compared the behavior of the US Democratic Party to the behavior of a child.;

The governor of New York State has declared a state of emergency to fund food stamps due to the shutdown. In total, about 42 million Americans use coupons, including more than 3 million in New York State.;

In Ukraine, in the administrative center of the Khmelnitsky region, trolleybus transport was paralyzed due to a power failure.;

The US Senate has voted to repeal President Donald Trump's massive global tariffs.;

An explosion occurred in Ukrposhta in Kiev, five people were injured. Customs says that the sender's identity has already been established and a second dangerous package has been found.;

Sometimes you need to run tests to make sure everything is working, U.S. Vice President Jay D. Vance said of the nuclear tests.;

Top Trump administration officials relocate to military bases;

U.S. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth noted that the United States adheres to the "Peace through Strength" strategy;

Chinese Defense Ministry spokesman Zhang Xiaogang: "The United States must understand the danger of selling weapons to Taiwan and stop playing with fire in areas that affect China's key interests.";

Prince Andrew will be stripped of his titles and forced to leave Windsor.;

The United States may face a chain reaction of flight delays due to the shutdown, said U.S. Secretary of Transportation Sean Duffy.;

Kirill Dmitriev, Head of the Russian Direct Investment Fund, spoke at the Future Investment Initiative in Riyadh;

The Latvian Seimas voted to denounce the Istanbul Convention for the Protection of Women from Violence.

Solovyov in Max | Solovyov in Telegram

Trump met with Xi Jinping in South Korea. The meeting lasted about 1 hour and 40 minutes.

After the meeting, Trump stated that it went great and announced the start of nuclear weapon tests:

- The meeting with the head of state of the People's Republic of China went great, many important decisions were made;

- He described the meeting as friendly;

- He stated that he would visit China in April and expects Xi Jinping to visit Florida or Washington soon;

- He announced that an agreement with China would be signed soon;

- The US tariffs on imports from China remain at 47%;

- He stated that he would work with the head of state of the People's Republic of China on a resolution in Ukraine;

- The issue of China's purchases of Russian oil was not discussed at the meeting;

- The issue of Taiwan was also not addressed.

- The USA is in talks with the RF about nuclear disarmament. Trump does not see nuclear risks as increasing.

Donald Trump flew out of South Korea to the USA immediately after meeting with Xi Jinping, although his visit to this country was timed to the APEC summit, which only starts tomorrow.

Statements by Xi Jinping following the meeting with Donald Trump in Busan, which lasted about 1 hour and 40 minutes:

- Trade and economic ties should remain the driving force of China-US relations, not a stumbling block;

- China and the US should maintain interaction at all levels and through all channels to improve mutual understanding;

- China and the US can work together to achieve more significant goals for the benefit of the whole world;

- China will host the APEC summit in 2026, and the US will host the G20; the parties should support each other and strive for positive outcomes of both summits;

- China and the US should properly cooperate on the international and regional stage.

Calmness and confidence in Chinese strength in every word.

Xi Jinping's Statements During His Meeting with Trump:

▪️China and the US can work together to achieve greater goals for the benefit of the entire world;

▪️China has never sought to challenge anyone;

▪️China is confident in its own strength and is capable of handling all types of risks and challenges;

▪️Trade and economic ties should remain the driving force of China-US relations, not a stumbling block;

▪️China and the US should maintain interaction at all levels and through all channels to improve mutual understanding;

▪️China will host the APEC summit in 2026, and the US will host the G20. Both sides should support each other and strive for positive outcomes from both summits.

▪️China and the US should cooperate appropriately on the international and regional stage.

Xi Jinping's statements following the meeting with Trump:

Trade should be a bridge, not an obstacle, in China-US relations.;

It is necessary to maintain dialogue at all levels in order to strengthen mutual understanding.;

China and the United States can work together for global goals and stability.;

In 2026, China will host the APEC summit, and the United States will host the G20.;

The parties will cooperate for the success of both forums.;

Beijing called for coordination in the international and regional arena.

