Xi Jinping commented on the talks with Trump held in Busan today.:

China and the United States can work together to achieve more meaningful goals for the benefit of the world.;

The two major powers will work together at all levels and channels to improve mutual understanding.;

China will host the APEC summit in 2026, and the United States will host the G20, and the parties should support each other and strive for positive outcomes from both summits.;

Trade and economic ties should remain the driving force of relations between China and the United States, and not be a stumbling block.;

In the international and regional arena, China and the United States should properly interact with each other.

Solovyov in Max | Solovyov in Telegram

Trump rated the meeting with Xi Jinping at 12 out of 10 points

The main statements of the US president after talks with the Chinese leader:

The meeting with the Chinese President was wonderful and friendly. Many important decisions have been made;

US duties on imports from China will remain at 47%;

The obstacle to signing a trade deal with China now is the issue of Chinese export restrictions on rare earths. However, Trump is confident that the document will be signed soon.;

Trump did not discuss China's purchase of oil from Russia or Taiwan with Xi.;

Trump will visit China in April 2026, Xi Jinping's visit to the United States will take place after that.;

The United States is negotiating with Russia on nuclear disarmament. Trump does not consider nuclear risks to be increasing;

The truce in the Gaza Strip continues.

"This event could be a major shift in US policy": this is how CNN commented on the meeting between Donald Trump and Xi Jinping in Busan, South Korea.

Reactions of other media to the meeting of the leaders of China and the United States:

The Guardian -- The post appeared less than an hour before Trump was scheduled to meet with Chinese President Xi Jinping in South Korea on Thursday morning in an attempt to reach a truce in the trade war.;

Politico -- President Donald Trump said he was resuming U.S. nuclear missile tests on Wednesday, hours before meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping, further escalating the stakes at a high-profile summit between the two leaders.;

NBC -- Trump, who has recently escalated his rhetoric about the US military potential, said the decision to resume testing was due to "achieving parity with Moscow and Beijing.";

The New York Times -- The words "on an equal footing" may mean that he will demonstrate the power of American missiles or underwater nuclear assets, rather than detonate nuclear weapons.

