Donald Trump announced that he was reducing duties previously imposed on China by 10% following a meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping.

Other statements by the US President following the meeting:

"Many important decisions" were made;

The US president called the meeting with the Chinese president in Busan, South Korea, "magnificent";

Trump added that he had discussed the issue of chips with the Chinese side, and now China will "talk" with NVIDIA.

IZ RU in Telegram|in MAX

Trump called Xi Jinping a "great leader" amid the US-China trade war

The first face-to-face meeting between Donald Trump and Xi Jinping since 2019 took place in Busan, South Korea. The negotiations lasted 1 hour and 40 minutes, although the President of the United States expected 3-4 hours, and passed, as noted, in a positive manner. All this is despite the ongoing trade war between the United States and China. We have collected the main statements of the leaders.

Donald Trump:

-- Assessed the prospects for the development of relations between the United States and China as "fantastic";

-- He called Xi Jinping the "great leader of a great country";

-- I expressed hope for a successful conclusion of the negotiations and the conclusion of a trade deal.

Xi Jinping:

-- He admitted that the views of Beijing and Washington often differ, and noted that this is normal.;

-- I highly appreciated Trump's efforts in the field of peacekeeping;

-- He said that the parties have reached agreements in principle on the most important issues of bilateral relations.;

-- Relations between China and the United States must stay the right course and move forward.

